cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the released datasets, please cite the following."
title: "CYP-Atlas + HDI-GNN: mechanism-grounded herb–drug interaction risk across the phytochemical space"
abstract: >-
  Software and frozen data releases for predicting herb–drug interaction (HDI)
  risk. CYP-Atlas trains per-enzyme CYP450/P-gp inhibition models on public
  ChEMBL bioactivity data, predicts a CYP-inhibition atlas over ~18k IMPPAT
  phytochemicals, and derives mechanistic, patient-specific HDI risk validated
  against curated HDI pairs. HDI-GNN is a structure-based graph neural network
  and baseline benchmark over a curated seed of cited herb–drug interactions.
type: software
